      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "MASt3R 3D Reconstruction — Up to 10 Images\n\nHOW TO LOAD IMAGES (1 to 10 photos of the same scene):\n  • Two Load Image nodes (#1, #2) are ENABLED by default. Click 'choose file to upload' on each and pick photos taken from different angles.\n  • To use MORE images: right-click any greyed-out Load Image node (#3 through #10) → Mode → Always, then upload a photo.\n  • To turn one off again: right-click → Mode → Never.\n  • The MASt3R Image Batch node automatically gathers all enabled images.\n\nTIPS FOR GOOD RECONSTRUCTIONS:\n  • Move your position between shots (sideways, not just rotating the camera).\n  • 30-60% overlap between adjacent images works best.\n  • Same camera/lens for all shots → keep shared_intrinsics = true.\n\nVRAM ON 8GB / RTX 4070:\n  • 2-3 images @ image_size=384: comfortable.\n  • 4-6 images @ image_size=384: tight; drop to 256 if you OOM.\n  • 7-10 images @ image_size=384: switch scenegraph_type from 'complete' to 'swin' (winsize ≈ 3) or 'oneref' to avoid quadratic blow-up.\n\nThe reconstructed 3D scene + camera frustums appear in the Preview 3D node on the right when the run finishes."
      ]
    },
